      "result": {
        "summary": "The diff meets the acceptance criteria. Pool.planner_pin() backs both Pool.pick and the CLI. The pin returns unconditionally for the planner role, and an unknown or missing id falls through to least-loaded selection. Other roles are unaffected, and the new pool test checks that pick('scout') ignores the pin. The CLI prints the stderr notice only when the pinned account is cooling or over budget, and still prints the account line and exits 0. The pool.toml example line is commented out. Rule 9 is byte-identical in CLAUDE.md and planner.md, and the old 'names' phrase now counts 0 in both. Both new tests are unittest methods with the acceptance names. I did not run the tests.",
